{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/223","id":4818063493,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTEdTLM8AAAABHy3QhQ","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/223","diff_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/223.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/223.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/223","number":223,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prove corrected finite terminal accounting with public canaries and shared Book mapping","user":{"login":"jicheng9617","id":74550583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTUwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74550583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617","html_url":"https://github.com/jicheng9617","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The corrected terminal accounting for the optimistic FTRL/BTRL source repairs needs a finite algebra identity that retains the final potential gap. This adds `OnlineCumulativePotential.finite_regret_identity` to the shared library/root and maps its single canonical declaration into the Online Learning Book. The equality includes every regularizer drift and the terminal gap; arbitrary real functions and an arbitrary carrier are allowed, with a positive natural horizon and an explicit terminal splice.\n\nTwo public canaries actually apply the same theorem: a one-round positive-gap counterexample to dropping the gap, and a two-round example with nonzero drift and a terminal point different from the unused original coordinate. Both are imported by shared `Tests`.\n\nValidation on clean source commit `7b372d79fcd3228d8d2cece73ad0181f94a70cf1`: shared Lean root and Tests, complete `tools/bandit.py check` (474 Python tests, 7 specified skips), contributor contract, process-memory checker, isolated Lean-verified site build and site checker all passed. Public import/axiom audits report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. Structural QA preserved all 11,104 existing declaration nodes and all 22 earlier source cards; the registry adds one declaration. Actual local Edge rendering checks the full frozen header, formulas, source links and chapter boundary. Exact raw receipts, failed preparation attempts, independent reviews, and original screenshots are retained under `runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/`.\n\nThis closes only the reviewed finite-real algebra subclause. The corrected source parents for Theorem 7.47 and Theorem 15.31 remain open, including extended-real/domain transport, actual algorithm producers, ghost attainment, support qualification, strong-convex stability, and Young bounds. The 7 required Chapter 2 containers and 6 future mathematical claims remain open; Chapter 2 stays partial with no complete denominator, and the Chapters 1–16 Goal remains active. No main, deployed site, chapter acceptance, whole-loop acceptance, or PURIFIED state is claimed.\n\nStacked on draft PR #221, exact base `b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8`. Later delivery commits append historical evidence only and preserve the gated active source byte-for-byte. Source: Orabona arXiv:1912.13213v10, printed pages 129–130 and 266–267 (PDF pages 141–142 and 278–279); the source corrections and finite-real specialization are explicitly distinguished from the printed full results.\n","created_at":"2026-10-11T09:29:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T09:29:42Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"05d6c55f87186c797e89543037b4e6498bb3d2a1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/223/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/223/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/223/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/statuses/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","head":{"label":"DakeBU:codex/research-online-ch2-b4-finite-identity","ref":"codex/research-online-ch2-b4-finite-identity","sha":"c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","user":{"login":"DakeBU","id":159223240,"node_id":"U_kgDOCX2NyA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159223240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/received_events","type":"User","user